    <string name="repair_mock_greeting_response">Hello! I’m your Wattson repair assistant. I can help you diagnose and solve problems with your devices.\n\nDescribe the issue you’re facing and, if possible, include the brand and model.</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_washing_machine_response">For your washing machine, here are a few diagnostic steps:\n\n1. Check the drain filter. A blocked filter can cause spinning or draining issues.\n2. Inspect the door seal. A worn seal can cause leaks.\n3. Clean the detergent drawer. Residue can block the water supply.\n4. Check the drain hose. It should not be bent or clogged.\n\nWhat symptom do you see exactly?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_dishwasher_response">For a dishwasher, the most common issues are:\n\n1. Dishes not cleaned properly. Check the spray arms for blockages and clean the filter.\n2. Standing water. Clean the filter and inspect the drain pump.\n3. Unusual noise. Make sure nothing is blocking the spray arms.\n4. Leak. Inspect the door seal and the water inlet hose.\n\nWhat problem are you having?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_refrigerator_response">For your fridge or freezer:\n\n1. Not cooling anymore. Check the thermostat and clean the rear condenser.\n2. Excessive frost. The door seal may be worn out.\n3. Unusual noise. The compressor or fan may be involved.\n4. Water leak. Check the defrost tray and drain hose.\n\nCan you describe the symptom a bit more?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_noise_response">An unusual noise can have several causes:\n\n- Clunking: foreign object, worn dampers, or a loose part.\n- Buzzing: pump or motor, often caused by a blocked drain pump.\n- Squeaking: bearings to replace or a worn belt.\n- Vibrations: appliance not level or an unbalanced load.\n\nCan you describe the noise more precisely and when it happens?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_leak_response">Water leaks can come from:\n\n1. Door seal. Check its condition and clean it with white vinegar.\n2. Water inlet hose. Inspect the fittings and tighten them if needed.\n3. Drain hose. Make sure it is attached properly and not pierced.\n4. Too much detergent. Excess product can cause overflow.\n\nWhere does the leak seem to come from?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_power_response">If your device does not turn on:\n\n1. Check the outlet. Test it with another device.\n2. Check the breaker. It may have tripped.\n3. Inspect the power cord. Do you see any damage?\n4. Power button. Make sure it works properly.\n5. Internal fuse. Some devices have a protective fuse.\n\nHave you checked these points? What kind of device is it?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_display_response">For a display issue:\n\n- Black screen: check the power supply and the HDMI or DisplayPort cable.\n- Dead pixels: often hard to repair, but a pixel massage tool can help.\n- Flickering: check the cable and refresh-rate settings.\n- Lines on screen: the display cable may need replacement.\n\nWhat kind of display issue do you have?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_battery_response">For battery issues:\n\n1. Reduced battery life. After two to three years, capacity naturally drops. Calibrate the battery with a full discharge and full recharge.\n2. Not charging anymore. Try another cable or charger. Clean the charging port.\n3. Unusual heat. Avoid using the device while charging. If it continues, the battery may need replacement.\n\nWhich device is affected?</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_thanks_response">You’re welcome. If you have other questions about maintaining or repairing your devices, feel free to ask. I’m here to help you extend their lifespan.</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_cost_response">Repair cost depends on several factors:\n\n- Type of failure: replacement part or a simple adjustment.\n- Spare part: price varies depending on brand and model.\n- Labor: if you use a repair professional.\n\nDescribe the issue and the device involved, and I can give you an estimate.</string>
    <string name="repair_mock_default_response">I understand. To help you better, could you give me a bit more detail?\n\n- Which device is involved? Brand and model if possible.\n- What exact symptom do you see?\n- Since when has the problem appeared?\n\nWith this information, I can suggest a more accurate diagnosis.</string>

